    "result_text": "There is only one test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a `checkDigit` field on the created-owner response equal to a Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`.\n\nChanges (3 files):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `checkDigit` accessor.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained utility with a single static `of(String)` method implementing the Luhn check digit exactly as the test's `luhn` helper does (rightmost digit doubled, non-digits skipped).\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line deriving `checkDigit` from `customerCode` (null-safe for list/collection mappings), alongside the existing computed fields like `membershipNumber`.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: the new behaviour lives in its own tiny class (zero surrounding complexity), and the only existing method touched was the mapper's `toOwnerDto` declaration, extended by a single annotation line rather than growing any method body.",
